Why: Background per-character typing on Windows (the WM_CHAR route native and XAML editors such as Notepad use) never watched for the user's own input and ran under a fixed 30 s provider deadline, so a long text kept typing after the user moved the mouse or pressed a key and then ended with a vague provider timeout. Count the user's own (not injected) mouse events including pointer motion and keyboard events, check them before every character and stop at once with a reply saying how much was typed; size the deadline to the text and say plainly how far typing got when it is reached.

